      "content": "The difference is rooted in perceived cultural origins and established social hierarchies. \"Old money\" signals inherited status, often associated with traditional, established European or American elite circles, which carries an automatic weight of pedigree. Reggaeton, while incredibly popular, is fundamentally tied to contemporary, often working-class or immigrant urban scenes, which the traditional luxury market views as less \"refined.\" The linguistic and stylistic markers are less about quality and more about association—one speaks of inherited tradition, the other of modern, vibrant, but less established street energy.",
