      "content": "that makes sense from a branding angle. so if we were looking at the actual language used in these groups—like the difference between the vocabulary in drill/mumble rap versus the \"quiet luxury\" crowd—is there a correlation between the linguistic complexity of the slang and the social status of the people using it? like, would a brand researcher view certain ethnic-based slang as inherently being \"lower-brow\" or less \"intellectual\" than more standard or formal dialects?",
